\title{#{f^*} minimises risk}
\taxon{Theorem}
\date{2026-01-15}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{Let #{\mu} be realisable. Then #{f^*} is the function that minimises risk. In particular, for all #{\varepsilon > 0}, #{f^*} has the property that}

##{\mathcal{R}(f^*) \leq \inf_{h \in \mathcal{F}} \mathcal{R}(h) + \varepsilon.}
